.TH VIBEOS-LAUNCHER 1 "2026-11-16" "vibeos 0.1.0" "VibeOS"
.SH NAME
vibeos-launcher \- the VibeOS home screen of VibeOS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B vibeos-launcher
.SH DESCRIPTION
VibeOS is a Wayland client drawn with Vulkan, or with OpenGL ES 3.0 when the GPU has no Vulkan driver: home pages with a dock, the app drawer, widgets, icon packs and parallax wallpapers. It is started by the vibeos GNOME Shell extension, which makes its window the desktop, and is not meant to be run by hand. Its settings are the GSettings schema vibeos.Shell.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B VIBEOS_LAUNCHER_RENDERER
.B vulkan
or
.BR gl :
draw with that renderer and no other. Without it, the launcher takes Vulkan when the Vulkan loader has a GPU that can present to the screen, otherwise OpenGL ES, and Vulkan's software rasterizer only when neither is there.
.TP
.B VIBEOS_DENSITY
Device pixels per Android dp, instead of the compositor's scale.
.TP
.B VIBEOS_WINDOWED
Run in a normal window rather than full screen (for development).
.SH SEE ALSO
gnome-shell(1)
